{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2910","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2910","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2910\",\"parent_revision\":\"580553bf65bc214be0652f3b6871f99a347a705d4eb2d641cf5978d075b4c9fe\",\"root_revision\":\"580553bf65bc214be0652f3b6871f99a347a705d4eb2d641cf5978d075b4c9fe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFinding from independent review of PR #2902. _stable_reference()'s last-resort key (hashlib.sha256(item.title.encode()).hexdigest()) is deterministic per title, so two work items sharing a title (including two items both with an empty title) hash to the identical key. In load_records() (github_work_items.py), both would compute the same reference and the second write to records_by_reference[reference] silently overwrites the first \u2014 one item vanishes from list_work_items()/get_work_item() results, with filesystem/glob iteration order deciding which survives. This narrows (from all-unreferenced-items collide) but does not eliminate the exact 'last-one-wins under a colliding key' bug class PR #2902 fixed for the reference='' case. No test in test_github_reference_healing.py exercises two items with duplicate or blank titles under the hash-fallback path. Related to #2909 (move reference derivation to the model layer) \u2014 may be resolved as part of that work, or fixed independently with a more collision-resistant fallback (e.g. include item creation timestamp or a stored UUID).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bug(backlog-mcp): _stable_reference()'s title-hash fallback still collides on duplicate/empty titles** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1381af92390a95d1b4c9f163db116f98180871173a8ccfc8196fb10b6677c5da\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS7K_A\"}"}